id: pm-lwnifd
title: Exact-tag Release recovery must bootstrap tracker gates and publish an unpublished immutable tag from its tagged source
description: "Auto Release run 30993783230 successfully created the sole v2026.8.5 tag, but downstream Release run 30994468126 checked out that tag without installing clone-local merge drivers. quality:static then observed five undeclared merge-driver warnings plus derived integrity and missing-link populations and stopped before npm publication. The current workflow_dispatch recovery intentionally checks current main and refuses a missing npm version, so it cannot recover a tag that exists immutably but never reached the registry."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:release",ci-parity,exact-tag-recovery,immutable-release,merge-safety,npm
created_at: "2026-08-05T09:54:50.481Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-05T10:22:04.109Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#96b2f4f37551cb3935f93353"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Every Release checkout builds and installs clone-local merge drivers before tracker-bearing static quality; workflow_dispatch distinguishes an already-published access recovery from an unpublished exact-tag recovery using an authenticated exact-version probe; an unpublished recovery checks out the existing immutable tag and may publish only that exact tagged source, while a published recovery keeps the reviewed main-source access repair behavior; version/tag guards fail closed for tagged-source publication; executable workflow contracts cover source selection, bootstrap ordering, and publication refusal; v2026.8.5 is recovered without creating or moving a second same-day tag and verifies through npm, npx, bunx, and GitHub Release"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make downstream Release clean-checkout prerequisites and immutable-tag recovery honest and recoverable
value: A daily tag cannot become permanently unpublished because its tag-push runner lacked clone-local configuration
impact: Closes the final gap between Auto Release preflight and the downstream publish workflow without weakening tracker ratchets or moving immutable tags
outcome: The sole daily tag is either published successfully or recoverable from its exact tagged source with the same mandatory gates
why_now: "v2026.8.5 exists, its release job failed before npm publication, and the one-release-per-day invariant forbids a replacement tag"
parent: pm-e70zh5
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: critical
environment: "GitHub Actions Auto Release run 30993783230, Release run 30994468126, tag v2026.8.5, npm registry"
repro_steps: "Run the tag-push Release workflow for v2026.8.5. quality:static reaches tracker measurement without clone-local merge drivers and fails validate_merge_driver_configuration; dispatch recovery from main then refuses because npm 2026.8.5 is absent."
resolution: Pending hosted merge and exact-tag production recovery; local implementation and gates are complete.
expected_result: "The existing v2026.8.5 tag passes the reviewed current Release workflow, publishes exactly @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.5, verifies npm/npx/bunx consumers, and creates one GitHub Release without moving or replacing the tag."
actual_result: Local workflow implementation and all required gates pass; production exact-tag recovery remains pending until the reviewed workflow change merges.
